# Board patches for xnu-12377 — the same series as patches/xnu-12377/series, minus the three
# patches whose board hooks have no definition in a RELEASE build.
#
# Why: emit_prelink.py needs a symbol-bearing RELEASE comparison kernel
# (profiles/os/ipados-27.0.1-24A446, extra_args --fileset-reference), and
# scripts/build-fileset-release-reference.py force-links only corecrypto, libpthread,
# ArmDTPlatform and ArmCpu — never the board archives. Any patch that calls a board symbol
# therefore has to compile with the symbol undefined, and these three do call board symbols:
#
#   uke-usb-pm-trace.patch        -> uke_usb_pm_snapshot       (IOServicePM)
#   uke-vm-init-checkpoints.patch -> uke_boot_stage{,_bind,_unbind} (arm_init/arm_vm_init)
#   uke-outside-dram-wc.patch     -> uke_boot_stage            (arm_vm_init)
#
# They are diagnostics (boot checkpoints, PowerManagement tracing, WC PTE attributes for the
# outside-DRAM window) and none of them is on the DWC3 enumeration path. They come back when
# the display and PM rounds bring their archives, because then the definitions exist in both
# builds. The list below is otherwise byte-identical to patches/xnu-12377/series.
#
native-ptrauth-null-portability.patch

